      "id": "IK-14884716:L80",
      "source_document": "14884716",
      "original_line": 80,
      "text": " 4. In reply, the learned counsel for the Respondents states that in the first instance, all issues raised in this petition are covered by the judgement dated 12.04.2023 passed by a Coordinate Bench of this Court in CM(M) 336/2023 with respect to the other sub-tenants; and this Court should not differ from Signature Not Verified Digitally Signed CM(M) 380/2023 Page 3 of 13 By:Rashmi Dabas Signing Date:20.10.2023 10:34:02 the said judgement as the facts in these cases are identical. 4.1.",
