    {
      "id": "IK-14884716:L99",
      "source_document": "14884716",
      "original_line": 99,
      "text": " Without prejudice to the above submissions and without in any manner admitting the allegations made by the- petitioner in the petition, it is submitted that there is no sub-letting, parting with or assignment of the premises in suit or any part thereof by respondent No. 1 in favour of respondents No. 2 to 6. In this behalf, it is submitted that the respondents No.2 to 6 named above have been using different portions of the premises in suit merely as a licensees.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "14884716",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/14884716/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-14884716-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "ba7944f4cf5c9b54f09efe24e80b7b2f1d45606c9076b55ba3e0bd3b2e8b5a05",
          "raw_char_range": [
            11506,
            11973
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            11715,
            12182
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 91,
          "original_line": 99
        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-14884716:L99",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 467
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-14884716:L100",
      "source_document": "14884716",
      "original_line": 100,
      "text": "None of the said users have claimed any hostile title or right of possession of any portion of the property in suit being used by them as licensees, much less to the exclusion of respondent No.1/tenant. The legal possession of the entire premises in suit continues to vest with the respondent No.1. There does not exist any relationship of landlord and tenant between the respondent No.1 on the one hand and on the other hand the respondents No.2 to 6 or anyone of them.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "14884716",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/14884716/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-14884716-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "ba7944f4cf5c9b54f09efe24e80b7b2f1d45606c9076b55ba3e0bd3b2e8b5a05",
          "raw_char_range": [
            11980,
            12450
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            12189,
            12659
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 92,
          "original_line": 100
        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-14884716:L100",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 470
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-14884716:L101",
      "source_document": "14884716",
      "original_line": 101,
      "text": "There is no subletting, assignment of tenancy rights or parting with of the tenanted premises or any part thereof by the respondent No.1 in favour of anyone, much less the Signature Not Verified Digitally Signed CM(M) 380/2023 Page 5 of 13 By:Rashmi Dabas Signing Date:20.10.2023 10:34:02 respondents No. 2 to 6. It is submitted that the respondents No.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "14884716",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/14884716/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-14884716-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "ba7944f4cf5c9b54f09efe24e80b7b2f1d45606c9076b55ba3e0bd3b2e8b5a05",
          "raw_char_range": [
            12457,
            12810
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            12666,
            13019
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 93,
          "original_line": 101
        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-14884716:L101",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 353
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-14884716:L102",
      "source_document": "14884716",
      "original_line": 102,
      "text": "2 to 6 have been paying license fee by way compensation for using the portion of the property to the petitioner and mere description of such compensation as \"rent\" is of no consequence inasmuch as the said word \"rent\" has been used in generic terms and in fact the same implies the payment of the compensation/license fee by respondents No.2 to 6 for using the portion in their respective use.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "14884716",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/14884716/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-14884716-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "ba7944f4cf5c9b54f09efe24e80b7b2f1d45606c9076b55ba3e0bd3b2e8b5a05",
          "raw_char_range": [
            12817,
            13210
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            13026,
            13419
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 94,
          "original_line": 102
        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-14884716:L102",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 393
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-14884716:L103",
      "source_document": "14884716",
      "original_line": 103,
      "text": "It is thus incorrect to allege that the respondent No.1 has sub-let, assigned or parted with possession of the premises in suit or any portion thereof in favour of the respondents No. 2 to 6 or anyone else. The present petition is without any merit. The present petition of the petitioner is malafide and the same is liable to be dismissed.\"",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "14884716",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/14884716/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/rgcn-data-expansion-09/continuation-01/open-14884716-0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "ba7944f4cf5c9b54f09efe24e80b7b2f1d45606c9076b55ba3e0bd3b2e8b5a05",
          "raw_char_range": [
            13217,
            13558
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            13426,
            13767
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 95,
